(defxdoc deftreemap-implementation
  :parents (deftreemap)
  :short "Implementation of @(tsee deftreemap)."
  :long
  (xdoc::topstring
   (xdoc::p
    "This book is included by @('centaur/fty/deftypes')
     like the other type generators,
     but it does not include the treemap library:
     the generator functions only build event forms,
     so the treemap functions and rules they mention are just quoted symbols
     (the treemap and treeset packages come from this book's portcullis).
     The library is instead supplied
     by the opt-in @('kestrel/fty/deftreemap') book,
     whose absence @('parse-flextreemap') detects with a friendly error.")
   (xdoc::p
    "A treemap member contributes <emph>three</emph>
     mutually recursive defines to a clique
     (deftypes appends per-member define lists):
     @('tree-all-keys-<name>') and @('tree-all-vals-<name>'),
     one structural fold over the raw binary tree per projection,
     and the public recognizer,
     which conjoins @('treemap::mapp') with both folds' first levels
     inlined at @('(treemap::fix x)').
     The inlining lets the clique admit with plain @('acl2-count') measures,
     since the folds are only ever applied to proper subtrees.
     Since a mutual recursion takes only one goal hint
     for its joint termination and guard proofs,
     the first fold define carries the hints for the whole clique.
     Two folds rather than one fused walk keep the bridges below
     single-predicate; the recognizer's extra pass is in line with
     @('treemap::mapp')'s own multi-pass checks, and neither fold builds
     a key or value treeset.")
   (xdoc::p
    "The theorems about the recognizer
     and count over the treemap operations
     are obtained by functional instantiation
     of the library's generic theories
     (@('generic-typed') and @('generic-count') in @('kestrel/data/treemap')),
     through two local min/delete views of the recognizer
     (one per projection, each instantiating the one treeset element stub)
     and a local structural fold for the count.
     The min/delete view of the recognizer
     is also exported as a disabled @(':definition') rule.")))

